@startuml revoke-and-unbind
!theme plain
title Legacy readable-token view: Broker v0, design only: ending access, grant revocation, task end, account withdrawal, R-ALLSTOP node-wide freeze

actor "Person" as P
participant "Phone app / operator device key\nsecure element; biometric presence" as Phone
participant "Operator command\nswarma-operator; no harness or shell" as O
participant "Original requester principal" as R
participant "swarma-workspace-export\napproved executor; child UID; fixed environment; no network" as X
participant "swarma-dispatcher\nown service OS account" as D
participant "swarma-user-manager\nroot, no-argument sudo entry" as H
participant "swarma-credential-broker\nunprivileged broker service UID" as B
participant "swarma-session-host\nown service OS account; later" as SH

== Authenticate each narrowing operator act ==
alt Phone-first path
  Phone -> P: show exact act (who, actions, until)
  P -> Phone: single biometric confirmation
  Phone -> O: signed canonical act; SSH over tailnet, pinned key only; forced command
  O -> O: verify pinned phone signature for this act; no reuse for another act
else Terminal fallback (phone not required)
  P -> O: password-authenticated sudo into swarma-operator
  O -> O: timestamp_timeout=0; no NOPASSWD or cached ticket
end
note over P,O
  Authentication repeats for each operator act below.
  Narrowing needs no extra content-confirmation step.
  Widening needs exact content confirmation and is refused in agent sessions.
  Binary, wire format, domain/canonical bytes and phone-key lifecycle open (§18.15).
end note

== a grant is revoked ==
O -> B: revocation.put (signed revocation envelope, §6.4)
B -> B: verify swarma-credential-broker revocation/1 signature\nunder the state lock: write the new revocation state\n(temp file, flush, rename, flush directory), update memory
B --> O: acknowledged (only after the state is durable)
B -> B: dispatcher revocation.check: revoked for affected chains;\nnext lease/renewal: lease_grant_revoked for the lease chain,\nlease_caller_revoked for the caller chain (method-specific refusals)

== the task ends ==
D -> B: unbind: binding_id; original unbind effect request_id
B -> B: durable receiver intent, then end leases and close UID connections;\npersist result and removal tombstone before acknowledgement (§7.2)
B --> D: recorded result and current removal state
opt reply lost or receiver recovery
  D -> B: effect.observe: original request_id, unbind, canonical-argument digest
  B -> B: authenticate original caller / operator; serialize with receiver journal
  B --> D: recorded (result + current state) | pending | rolled_back |\nnot_recorded | unavailable | contradictory
  D -> D: only authoritative evidence proves absence; unknown holds claim
end
opt workspace-capable allocation: R-TRANSFER cleanup obligation
  D -> H: round end: account-wide journaled stop and confirm absence
  H --> D: account-wide absence evidence or unresolved result
  D -> D: workplace round write-fenced; no further tool calls into workspace
  alt confirmed absence; export admitted
    D -> X: export workspace data; no links followed; skip worker .git/history
    alt whole export succeeds
      X --> D: bounded change set
      D -> D: journal result digests and recorded export
      D --> R: recorded workspace result only to original requester
    else export refuses
      X --> D: whole-export refusal; no partial result
      D -> D: export cleanup obligation remains pending
    end
  else absence unconfirmed
    D -> D: no export; retain cleanup obligation
  end
  opt explicit operator waiver of export obligation
    O -> D: admitted operator act (format unpublished; e.g. after compromise)
    D -> D: record waiver; never silently drop export obligation
  end
  break neither export recorded nor operator waiver
    D -> D: retain home; no retirement deletion
  end
end
D -> H: user.retire {generation: 4a91c5e03b2d4788a649d70fc62e15bd}\n(abbreviated helper request; distinct retire effect ID)
H -> H: state retiring: launcher refuses 4a91c5e03b2d4788a649d70fc62e15bd;\nstop processes, verify quiescence; (v1: egress stays denied)
H -> H: declared-key cleanup; delete home;\nremove account and group; state removed
note over D,H
  R-TRANSFER export precedes home deletion unless operator explicitly waives it.
  Workspace data becomes a candidate only through board deterministic import;
  exact repository-signed commit reviewed/integrated through board's path.
  Reviewer: admitted review role; outside untrusted class; distinct from producer;
  trusted-class local agent placement or person holding the role (§12.1).
  Circle membership alone never grants review eligibility.
  Local-only reviewer and requester-exclusion policies remain open/off (§18.23).
  Separate retirement metadata export is service-generated closed-schema data
  without agent-controlled strings/names/links/bodies; not the workspace result.
  Explicit home retention needs authentication + content confirmation;\n  refused inside agent sessions; cannot guarantee confidentiality.
  Unbind tombstones remain for admissible retry/reconciliation (§7.2);
  expired/missing evidence is unavailable, never not_recorded.
end note
H --> D: removed
note over D,H: Future keeper integration (D-IDENTITY): after retirement,\ndispatcher separately revokes only identities registered as one-shot.\nStanding identities require a signed operator revocation through swarma-operator;\nunbind/retire are not blanket identity revocation.
note over B: a recycled UID or a repeated label inherits nothing:\nbindings, grants and leases are keyed by generation

== Independent direct operator retirement while broker is unavailable ==
O -> H: authenticated operator retirement through helper's local contract
H -> H: irreversible retiring ledger fence; local quiescence; deletion waits for recorded export or explicit waiver
H --> O: local retirement result; NOT a broker unbind receipt
O -> O: retain explicit durable unconfirmed binding-cleanup obligation
note over O,B
  Helper has no broker principal and makes no unbind RPC.
  Later dispatcher/operator reconciliation uses original unbind effect,
  effect.observe and tombstone. Retired generation refuses lease/renew;
  recycled UID inherits no authority (§7.3-§7.4).
  R-OUTCOME: pre-admission rejection has no intent; unfinished admitted
  unbind is pending and continues identical arguments, only narrowing.
  Terminal replay never removes a replacement binding (§13.2).
end note

== Node-wide emergency stop (R-ALLSTOP) ==
note over O,SH
  One narrowing act: phone authentication + one confirmation or password terminal;
  refused inside agent sessions. Same signed act identity/canonical content
  goes directly to each applicable operator intake; each verifies and journals.
  Prompt independent issue; no relay or wait behind per-generation stops.
  Intake/correlation/retry bounds unpublished (§18.17); design only.
end note
par Dispatcher part
  O -> D: direct admitted act
  alt dispatcher available
    D -> D: journal hold at act admission; close admission
  else absent / unready / mid-swap
    O -> O: dispatcher part unknown; retry and reconcile when available
  end
else Broker containment part
  O -> B: direct admitted act; does not depend on dispatcher
  B -> B: under state lock: durably journal freeze of all leases/renewals\nbefore acknowledgement; includes queued and post-refresh delivery
else User-manager containment part
  O -> H: direct admitted act (terminal path; phone transition unpublished)
  H -> H: persist receiver launch/create/activation fence before inventory;\nrange deny-all (R-RANGE-DENY); exclude already-issued starts
else Session-host part (later)
  O -> SH: direct admitted act
  SH -> SH: close delivery and snapshot bound boards; journal own part
end
O -> H: operator generation-scoped journaled stops when dispatcher unavailable\nissued after containment calls; do not wait for their replies
opt individual service evidence arrives independently of stop progress
  D --> O: own hold/journal result if available; otherwise unknown
  B --> O: own freeze evidence or unknown; no assertion about other services
  H --> O: own containment/stop evidence or unknown
  SH --> O: own evidence or unknown (later)
end
note over D,H
  Dispatcher initiates stops when available; helper journals termination.
  Stops follow containment issue, never wait for containment acknowledgements.
  Final account-wide absence requires receiver fence and closed inventory frontier.
  Dispatcher later reconciles operator-stopped outcomes; unknown retains claims.
end note
note over O,SH
  Per-service results; undeliverable parts unknown and retried independently.
  Broker reply unavailable with valid helper stop evidence: stops progress;
  broker part remains unknown, admission stays closed.
  Every durable part, including dispatcher hold/journal, required for whole-act
  completion/recovery; no success from process absence alone.
  Content-confirmed explicit recovery names stopped set / per-session restart scope;
  retain every independent gate; no automatic recovery or restart authority from broker.
  Revocation.check unavailable while frozen/unresolved; delivered tokens keep vendor lifetime.
  [[../spec/broker.md#155-node-wide-emergency-stop-r-allstop Spec §15.5]]
  Act/record/recovery formats and refusal codes unpublished (§18.17).
end note

== the account is withdrawn ==
O -> B: account.revoke {account: owner/claude/personal}
B -> B: account state revoked; subsequent leases / renewals refuse lease_account_revoked (§8.2)
P -> P: revoke at vendor (Claude web interface, §10.1);\ntokens already copied end only there or at expiry
note over B
  Broker owns account/secret, grant/revocation, binding and lease files;
  helper owns ledger and retirement. Record writes atomic (§12.4).
  Material-deletion procedure / account.revoke commit point:
  unspecified in spec §5.3 / §13.2.
  [[../spec/broker.md#64-revocation Spec §6.4]]
  [[lease-recovery.puml M-CB2: crash after durable revoke and fail-closed repair]]
  [[record-states.puml M-CB3: independent record states and transition gaps]]
end note
note over D,B
  R-LOCK: no state lock across synchronous platform-service calls (§13.1).
  Explicit authorised unbind is unaffected by elapsed expiry-removal gate.
  R-REBIND also ends old leases and retains old-binding tombstone;
  fresh-lease handoff remains open (§18.11).
end note
@enduml

@startuml revoke-and-unbind-secret-free
!theme plain
title Proposed secret-free view: revoke-and-unbind — inactive
actor "Authorized owner" as O
participant "Broker" as B
participant "Gateway" as G
participant "Action service" as E
participant "Session stop owner" as S
participant "Vendor lifecycle adapter" as V
O -> B : signed revocation / freeze / retirement / all-stop scope
B -> B : durable broker fence; no new lease/renewal/final material delivery
B --> O : broker part only; not consumer completion
G -> G : close scoped listener sessions, queues, cached use and streams
E -> E : close queued actions; interrupt started action if safe\notherwise finish and record actual outcome / UNKNOWN
G --> O : durable closure or unknown
E --> O : durable closure or unknown
note over B,E
  Propagation from signed publication: max(S + A, F), existing owning bounds.
  Completion: each consumer durably acknowledges OR its earlier authority expired.
  Intake ack, lease release and process stop are separate facts.
end note
== Independent possible-leak path ==
G -> G : block before forwarding
G -> B : narrowly authenticated detector trigger; not v0 lease report
B -> B : durable WHOLE-account hold; all generations / launches\nlease and renew check under lock; restart cannot bypass
G -> G : close all account listener sessions, queues and streams
E -> E : close account uses; record actual started-action outcomes
G -> S : authorized session stop; independently record outcome
opt confirmed leak under separately published criteria/contract
  B -> V : required vendor rotation / invalidation
end
note over O,V
  Possible leak never defaults to confirmed or authorizes vendor action.
  Only owner lifts hold; alerts cannot delay containment.
  Local release / use closure / session stop / vendor validity distinct.
end note

legend bottom
  Separate proposed secret-free mode, document revision 1: INACTIVE / UNQUALIFIED.
  Semantic responsibilities only; no new v0 methods, fields, codes or record formats.
  [[../spec/secret-free-mode.md Owning proposed contract and qualification gates]]
endlegend
@enduml
